In the IPCC AR6 scenario naming convention (e.g. SSP1-1.9, SSP2-4.5, SSP5-8.5), what do the labels denote?
#pagebreak()
#set page(width: a_width, height: auto, margin: a_margin)
#set text(size: a_size)
SSP number indicates climate model generation; hyphenated number indicates century
#pagebreak()
#set page(width: a_width, height: auto, margin: a_margin)
#set text(size: a_size)
SSP prefix denotes the socioeconomic storyline (1=Sustainability to 5=Fossil-fueled development); hyphenated number denotes the nominal radiative forcing in $"W/m"^2$ at year 2100
#pagebreak()
#set page(width: a_width, height: auto, margin: a_margin)
#set text(size: a_size)
The number indicates global mean sea level rise in meters by 2050
#pagebreak()
#set page(width: a_width, height: auto, margin: a_margin)
#set text(size: a_size)
The prefix represents atmospheric methane concentrations in ppm
